 "text": "Before 1846, surgery meant being awake for every second. October 16th, 1846. Boston, Massachusetts General Hospital. Dentist William Morton has a patient, Gilbert Abbott, breathe in ether. Surgeon John Collins Warren operates on a tumor in his neck while Abbott sleeps. Warren turns to the crowd. Gentlemen, this is no humbug. The room becomes known as the Ether Dome, the start of modern anesthesia. Every legend has a beginning.",
